# 1.3: PERFORM's 27 effects over MIDI. In: CC 20-31 the low octave's keys (0-11), CC 102-116 the fifteen above
# (12-26); 64 and over holds, under lets go; on any page, any channel. Out: an effect played by hand sends its CC on
# channel 16 (127, then 0), with MIDI out on; a CC's own effects are not sent back
wait 500
expect view 0
listen
expect fxcc 0
# in, on HOME: Stutter (key 0, CC 20), no page change, nothing sent back
midi B0 14 7F
wait 300
said Stutter
expect pcc 1
expect pnow 1
expect pheld 0
expect view 0
expect fxcc 0
# 63 lets go; 64 holds
midi B0 14 3F
wait 100
expect pcc 0
expect pnow 0
midi B3 14 40
wait 100
expect pcc 1
midi B3 14 00
wait 100
expect pcc 0
# the top run: Reverse (key 12, CC 102), Crush (key 26, CC 116); the CCs either side are no effect's
midi B0 66 7F
midi B0 74 7F
wait 300
said Reverse
# the link's STATE tells them
link hello
wait 400
expect lfx 67112960
expect pcc 67112960
midi B0 65 7F
midi B0 75 7F
midi B0 20 7F
wait 100
expect pcc 67112960
# all notes off lets them go
midi B0 7B 00
wait 100
expect pcc 0
expect pnow 0
expect store_writes 0
# in PERFORM a CC's effect flashes as a key's does, and its key goes dark
tap SEL
wait 300
expect view 17
midi B0 18 7F
wait 400
said Gate
expect pflash 1
expect litkey4 0
shot cc-gate.png
midi B0 18 00
wait 400
expect pflash 0
expect litkey4 1
# out: a key by hand, its CC on channel 16 (Half time: key 2, CC 22)
expect fxcc 0
key w1 down
wait 200
expect fxcc 1
expect fxcclast 5759
expect pnow 4
key w1 up
wait 200
expect fxcc 2
expect fxcclast 5632
# the top run: Crush (key 26, CC 116)
key w15 down
wait 200
expect fxcclast 29823
key w15 up
wait 200
expect fxcclast 29696
expect fxcc 4
# a CC held, PERFORM left: let go with the rest
midi B0 18 7F
wait 100
expect pcc 16
tap SEL
wait 300
expect pcc 0
expect pnow 0
expect fxcc 4
# the grid's effects that PERFORM has too send theirs: Reverb (the grid's ninth: w8; PERFORM's key 14, CC 104)
press REC
wait 500
key w8 down
wait 200
expect fxcc 5
key w8 up
release REC
wait 300
expect fxcc 6
# PERFORM's fourth knob is Chorus (1.3; Sweep is the Sequence's Move page's Width): by the knob, by CC 19 there, and
# by CC 80 anywhere; never saved; a new piece starts without it
tap SEL
wait 300
expect view 17
listen
midi B0 13 7F
wait 300
said Chorus 100
midi B0 13 00
wait 300
said Chorus Off
tap SEL
wait 300
expect chorus 0
midi B0 50 40
wait 300
expect chorus 50
expect view 0
expect store_writes 0
# a new piece starts without it
turn PRESET 1
wait 300
expect piece 1
expect chorus 0
